    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "DNG Royal County are delighted to present 39 Kilcarn Court, Navan, Co. Meath to the market. This spacious four-bedroom family home enjoys a quiet cul-de-sac setting within this mature and highly sought-after residential development, conveniently located just off the Old Dublin Road.\n\nThe property offers bright and well-proportioned accommodation throughout. The ground floor comprises an entrance hallway, a generous sitting room with feature fireplace, guest WC and a spacious open-plan kitchen/dining area to the rear, with direct access to the private enclosed garden. Upstairs, there are four well-proportioned bedrooms together with a family bathroom, providing comfortable and versatile accommodation for family living.\n\nTo the front, the property benefits from a driveway providing off-street parking, together with a garden partially laid in lawn and pedestrian side access to the rear. The rear garden is laid out in a combination of lawn and patio, providing an ideal space for outdoor dining, entertaining and family use. A particular advantage is that the property is not overlooked to the rear. \n\nKilcarn Court is a mature and well-established residential development in an exceptionally convenient Navan location. Navan Town Centre is within easy reach, offering an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and recreational amenities. Beaufort College, Gaelscoil Éanna, Navan Rugby Club and the Ardboyne Hotel are all located nearby.The property is also particularly well positioned for commuters, with convenient access to the M3 motorway via Junction 8, providing excellent connectivity to Dublin and the surrounding areas.\n\nCombining spacious four-bedroom accommodation, off-street parking, a private rear garden, quiet cul-de-sac setting and an excellent location, 39 Kilcarn Court represents a superb opportunity for those seeking a family home in a mature and highly convenient Navan neighbourhood.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n"
      },
      {
